        "text": "All Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here are the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] fetch_api_key.py**: Fetches an API key from Azure Key Vault.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] fetch_db_secret.py**: Fetches a database connection secret from Azure Key Vault.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] parse_json_secret.py**: Retrieves and parses a JSON-formatted secret from Azure Key Vault.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] rotate_secret_version.py**: Reads a specific secret version or staged value from Azure Key Vault.\n5. **[HELPER] security_client.py**: Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Azure Key Vault.\n6. **[HELPER] security_models.py**: Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Azure Key Vault.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] rotation_summary.py**: Summarizes secret rotation status using Azure Text Analytics.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] secret_label_safety.py**: Checks secret labels and notes for unsafe text using Azure Text Analytics.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] secret_audit_embedding.py**: Embeds secret audit notes for semantic search using Azure Text Analytics.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] runbook_translate.py**: Translates secret-rotation runbook notes using Azure Translator.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses Azure services and makes the provider identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.",
